= {arXiv:2608.23319v2} }[Button: Copy Citation]\nIn particular, the limiting dynamics are universal and do not depend on the higher-order details of the plaquette action.\n\n  * The Gao-Zhuang conjecture for the Heisenberg group over $\\mathbb{F}_p$\n\nYongke Qu, Guoqing Wang\n\nAug 25 2026 math.CO math.NT arXiv:2608.23319v2\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{2608.23319, author = {Yongke Qu and Guoqing Wang}, title = {{T}he {G}ao-{Z}huang conjecture for the {H}eisenberg group over $\\mathbb{{F}}_p$}, year = {2026}, eprint = {2608.23319}, note = {arXiv:2608.23319v2} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nLet $G$ be a finite nonabelian group. The small Davenport constant $\\mathsf d(G)$ of $G$ is the largest integer $\\ell$ such that there exists a product-one free sequence over $G$ of length $\\ell$, while the Gao constant $E(G)$ of $G$ is the least integer $\\ell$ such that every sequence over $G$ of length at least $\\ell$ contains a product-one subsequence of length exactly $|G|$. A long-standing conjecture of Gao and Zhuang \\citeZG2005 asserts that $E(G)=\\mathsf d(G)+|G|$ for every finite nonabelian group $G$. Let $p$ be an odd prime and let $H_{p^3}=\\operatorname{UT}_3(\\mathbb F_p)$ be the finite Heisenberg group over $\\mathbb F_p$. Godara and Sarkar proved the Gao-Zhuang equality for $H_{27}=\\operatorname{UT}_3(\\mathbb F_3)$ and asked whether the same equality holds for $H_{p^3}$ for every odd prime $p$. Recently, Volkmann proved that $\\mathsf d(H_{p^3})=3p-3$. In this paper, we determine the Gao constant of $H_{p^3}$ and prove that $E(H_{p^3})=\\mathsf d(H_{p^3})+|H_{p^3}|=p^3+3p-3$. Together with the known abelian and cyclic-index cases, this completes the verification of the Gao-Zhuang equality for all groups of order $p^3$, for every prime $p$.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMachina Mathematica (https://lean.up.railway.app/)\nciteturn3search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; PM2  |